# Operator custody (testnet demo).
# This backend holds no Stellar secret key. Do not put one in this file.
# The signer holds one key for each operator role. Each role has its own wallet.
#
#   admin     close, set_wiring, set_eligible, set_enforced, mint_batch
#   servicer  distribute (it pays the collections in the deal asset, so it needs a trustline)
#   reporter  set_rate on the rate oracle
#   crank     push_batch on the paying agent, and the wasm uploads and the
#             contract deploys of pnpm deal:deploy (it holds only XLM)
#
# The signer of the operator roles:
#   dfns         the production custody (the default). See the Dfns settings below.
#   stellar-cli  a development signer for the testnet demo without Dfns. The
#                keystore of the local Stellar CLI signs (stellar tx sign).
#                This backend still holds no secret: it knows only the
#                identity names. This signer refuses the public network.
# OPERATOR_SIGNER=dfns
# With OPERATOR_SIGNER=stellar-cli: the identity name of each role in the
# Stellar CLI keystore (stellar keys ls). Give the names, never the keys.
# CLI_ADMIN_IDENTITY=
# CLI_SERVICER_IDENTITY=
# CLI_REPORTER_IDENTITY=
# CLI_CRANK_IDENTITY=
#
# The service account credential key authenticates the API calls of this
# backend to Dfns. It cannot sign a Stellar transaction. Only a Dfns wallet
# signs, and only when the Dfns policy of that wallet lets it sign.
# The admin, servicer and reporter wallets have an approval policy. A person
# approves each of their signatures in app.dfns.io. The crank wallet has no
# approval policy.
#
# All settings below are optional. Without them the server starts read-only.
# A signed operation then fails with a message that names the missing setting.
# DFNS_API_URL=https://api.dfns.io
# DFNS_ORG_ID=
# DFNS_AUTH_TOKEN=
# DFNS_CRED_ID=
# The credential private key in PEM format. Write it on one line with \n
# between the lines, or on several lines between double quotes.
# DFNS_PRIVATE_KEY=
# DFNS_ADMIN_WALLET_ID=
# DFNS_SERVICER_WALLET_ID=
# DFNS_REPORTER_WALLET_ID=
# DFNS_CRANK_WALLET_ID=
#
# Horizon (classic operations and account reads).
# HORIZON_URL=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org
# The trustline asset of pnpm custody:trust comes from the deal asset
# contract: its name() is CODE:ISSUER. Set both values below only to
# override that asset.
# EURC_CODE=
# EURC_ISSUER=
#
# Optional real IPFS pinning (our CIDs match cidVersion=1)
# PINATA_JWT=
# TRANCHING_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
# Metadata encryption (AES-256-GCM) - seals the `confidential` section of NFT
# metadata before IPFS storage. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# Deleting the key = GDPR crypto-shredding (sealed sections become unreadable).
# METADATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# Bearer token for GET /metadata/:cid/clear (authorized data-room view)
# METADATA_VIEWER_TOKEN=
